      "value": "2",
      "quote": "On examination, the patient exhibited stiffness and frequent painful extensor spasms of the lower extremities provoked by tactile stimuli and voluntary movement of the extremities. Tone in the upper extremities was normal during passive movements, and there were no spasms or contractures in upper extremity or neck muscles. Passive head movements caused no discomfort. There was no appearance of fixed lumbar hyperlordosis, abnormal trunk extension, rigidity in abdominal muscles, or muscle hypertrophy.",
